      "source_assessment": "The paper distinguishes the environmental isolate codes Bo1/Bo2 and Ht3 from MALDI-TOF library best-match names. Bo1 and Bo2 are reported as Serratia marcescens, with best matches ZCF25 and UCP1549; Ht3 is reported as Bacillus mojavensis, with best match B1811. These matches neither equate the actual isolates to those library stocks nor assign their genomes to GTDB species. T2 and T3 each contain six isolates; the separate T4 benchmark does not enlarge either roster. Keep Bo1/Bo2 separate and preserve all four Pseudomonas stock descriptors and existing mappings; neither of the eight alternatives is selected as an actual study-stock identity. Preserve distinct optimization-screen, simulated-water and pesticide-panel contexts. Keep HPLC residue loss separate from mineralization and predicted enzyme inventory separate from actual genotype or pathway activity. Preserve the exact 94.30 percent and 57.88-to-3.30 mg/L T2 endpoint context in the original ledger; no count, library-score or probability is derived from native ambiguity options.",
